<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transport From Salem To Chennai</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p>Ensuring the secure and transparent handover of two-wheelers and motorcycles upon destination arrival is a critical phase in logistics operations. This process demands rigorous adherence to standard operating procedures to mitigate disputes and ensure customer satisfaction. The final delivery begins strictly during daylight hours, providing optimal visibility for a comprehensive physical inspection.</p>
<p>The delivery agent must conduct a detailed re-inspection of the vehicle’s exterior and interior, meticulously comparing its current state against the high-resolution photographs captured at the time of pickup. This step ensures that any new scratches, dents, or mechanical anomalies are identified immediately, allowing for clear documentation before the customer accepts the vehicle.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Beyond the visual assessment, verifying the odometer reading is a non-negotiable component of the handover protocol.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The agent must cross-reference the current mileage displayed on the motorcycle’s dashboard with the figures recorded in the Legal Metrology (LR) bilty or bill of lading.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Any discrepancy in the odometer reading must be flagged immediately, as it could indicate unauthorized usage during transit.</span></li></ul>
<p>This verification protects both the carrier and the recipient by establishing a factual baseline for the vehicle’s usage history. Consistency between the physical vehicle and the legal documentation is paramount to maintaining operational integrity.</p>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Once the visual inspection and odometer verification are complete and confirmed as accurate, the final step involves the formal execution of the condition sign-off.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The recipient must review the inspection report and the accompanying documents carefully.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Only after acknowledging the vehicle’s condition and the accuracy of the odometer reading should the customer sign the delivery receipt.</span></li></ul>
<p>This signed sign-off serves as the legal closure of the transit cycle, transferring responsibility for the vehicle’s condition from the logistics provider to the owner. Key elements of this final stage include:</p>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(230px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px;">
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #f59e0b22; color: #f59e0b; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">01</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 01</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Confirming all visible damage matches the pickup photos exactly.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 02</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Validating the odometer reading against the LR bilty entry.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 03</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Obtaining a clear, legible signature from the recipient.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Protocol 04</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Retaining a copy of the signed document for audit trails.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p>This structured approach minimizes post-delivery disputes and reinforces trust in the logistics network.</p></div>
